{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA + fix (option (a), /rebar-debug Phase 2) — change up for Gerrit review\n\n**Confirmed root cause (reproduced locally).** `pyproject.toml`'s `[agents]` extra declared `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries,duckduckgo]>=1.107,<2` with **no direct bound on the `anthropic` SDK**. An unlocked resolve floats anthropic to its latest release; anthropic **1.0.0+** switched its client to a vendored `httpx2` and rejects a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. The provider seam `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider` (line ~155-157) constructs `AsyncAnthropic(..., http_client=httpx.AsyncClient(...))`, so under a floated SDK it raises `TypeError: Invalid http_client argument; Expected an instance of httpx2.AsyncClient but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>`, cascading into ~90 failures. `uv.lock` (pins 0.121.0) masks it on the merge gate; only the unlocked mirror-sweep legs float.\n\n**RED evidence (this session):**\n- `uv pip compile` of `.[agents]` at BOTH highest and `--resolution lowest-direct` selected `anthropic==1.2.0` (+ `httpx2==2.12.0`) against the pre-fix pyproject.\n- Under `anthropic==1.2.0`, `AsyncAnthropic(api_key=…, max_retries=0, http_client=httpx.AsyncClient())` raised the exact `TypeError` above; under `anthropic==0.121.0` it constructed cleanly (`max_retries=0`).\n\n**httpx2 boundary — corrected from the ticket's initial \"<1.2.0\".** Verified against PyPI metadata: anthropic `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, `1.2.0` **all** declare `httpx2<3,>=2.0.0`; every `0.x` through `0.125.0` declares stdlib `httpx<1,>=0.25.0`. The first httpx2-vendoring release is **1.0.0**, so the correct ceiling is **`<1`** (a `<1.2.0` ceiling would still admit the broken 1.0.0/1.1.0).\n\n**Fix (pyproject + tests only):** added a direct `anthropic>=0.121.0,<1` to `[agents]`.\n- **Ceiling `<1`** — strictly below the first httpx2 release, so no resolve can float onto the rejected client.\n- **Floor `>=0.121.0`** is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` leg uses `--resolution lowest-direct`, which pins a *direct* constraint to its floor. `>=0.121.0` matches what `uv.lock` resolves and satisfies pydantic-ai-slim's own `anthropic>=0.108.0`, so the floor leg lands on the verified SDK instead of dropping to an ancient one.\n- **Post-fix resolutions:** highest → `anthropic==0.125.0`, lowest-direct → `anthropic==0.121.0` (both `0.x`, stdlib httpx). Both construct the provider without `TypeError`. (`httpx2` still appears in the tree — pulled by `genai-prices`, unrelated to anthropic — harmless; the break was anthropic *requiring* `httpx2.AsyncClient`, not its mere presence.)\n- Regenerated `uv.lock` (minimal: adds the direct anthropic requires-dist edge; anthropic stays pinned 0.121.0) so CI's `--locked` Verified gate stays consistent.\n\n**Defect origin (caused_by → 7d58-e88b-1643-4542, stun-ash-zeal).** This is an **omission**: no commit \"broke\" it — anthropic 1.0.0 vendored httpx2 externally. Story 7d58 introduced the uncapped `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic]` dependency in commit `75e598a41e7c`; its declared scope is \"pyproject.toml [agents] (add pydantic-ai-slim extras)\" and its file_impact includes pyproject.toml, so bounding the SDK fell within its scope. `75e598a` predates the `rebar-ticket:` trailer convention (names \"Story 7d58\" in prose), so the caused_by data-integrity gate is commit-less here; recorded via the sanctioned `--force=\"scope-of-work attribution: …\"` (that force is on the link gate, NOT a plan/close gate). Close class when the orchestrator closes: **preexisting** (a latent packaging omission that a later external SDK release activated; no rebar regression introduced it).\n\n**RED→GREEN test (`tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py::test_anthropic_sdk_is_bounded_below_the_httpx2_line`).** A pure pyproject-parse oracle (portable: no network, no install, no CI-provider trigger). It parses the declared direct `anthropic` requirement and asserts its specifier admits `0.121.0` (locked, stdlib-httpx) and rejects `1.0.0`/`1.1.0`/`1.2.0` (httpx2). Shown **RED first** against the unbounded pyproject (no direct anthropic dep → `assert None is not None`), then **GREEN** after the fix. **Mutation teeth (sandboxed, macOS `sandbox-exec`):** removing the `<1` ceiling makes the specifier admit `1.0.0` → test returns **RED**; restored → GREEN. Not a change-detector (asserts the observable packaging contract, not private names). `make lint` clean.\n\n**Scope confirmation — stayed out of eb64.** Diff is exactly `pyproject.toml` + `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` + `uv.lock`. Did **not** touch `src/rebar/llm/` (incl. `anthropic_model.py`), the reconciler, `_operation_config.py`, `_cli/`, `_commands/`, `_store/`, `.github/workflows/`, or `docs/adr/`. The provider-seam adaptation (option b) remains in follow-up `2bd6-ff87-d48c-4a65`.\n\n**Sibling census (Step 7).** The construct is \"a `pydantic-ai-slim[<provider>]` extra pulling an unbounded provider SDK.\" Parallel surfaces in pyproject: `pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` (unbounded `openai`), `pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]` (boto3). Not currently broken and out of this ticket's operator-approved scope: only the **anthropic** provider seam passes a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient` into a vendored-client SDK, and only anthropic legs are red. Flagged here for monitoring; not filed as confirmed siblings (unproven + would require touching provider seams that belong to eb64).\n\nLeaving `1f35` **in_progress** — close waits on `Verified +1` + `LLM-Review +1` per the orchestrator."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788113090134215004,"uuid":"d7108263-5a9c-431a-95d5-8d24804e497a"}